  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "What is the range of $y=2(5)^{x}-3?$",
  "worked_solution": "The range of ${5}^{x}$ is\n\n$$\n{5}^{x}>0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $2$ and then subtracting $3,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{x} & >0 \\\\ 2(5)^{x} & >0 \\\\ 2(5)^{x}-3 & >0-3 \\\\ y & >-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $y\\in (-3,\\infty ).$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $f(x)=2(5)^{x}-3$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943819/assets/c8179a12c8032d81ebbdb8a5a95c158e905fab4d24aa68f0eeef1f4bc4971a0b.png)",
